Subject: [PATCH] net: smsc911x: bound PHY loopback FIFO reads
Upstream-Status: Pending

The loopback receive length includes four FCS bytes, but the old buffer
reserved only the transmitted frame length. Worse, length validation ran
after the FIFO read. An unrelated queued frame could overwrite private
driver state. Align both buffers, reserve the FCS, and drain unexpected
lengths without copying them into the loopback receive buffer.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/smsc/smsc911x.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/smsc/smsc911x.c
@@ -120,2 +120,2 @@
-	char loopback_tx_pkt[MIN_PACKET_SIZE];
-	char loopback_rx_pkt[MIN_PACKET_SIZE];
+	char loopback_tx_pkt[MIN_PACKET_SIZE] __aligned(4);
+	char loopback_rx_pkt[MIN_PACKET_SIZE + 4] __aligned(4);
@@ -785,1 +785,12 @@
-		pdata->ops->rx_readfifo(pdata, (unsigned int *)bufp, rdsz);
+		if (pktlength != sizeof(pdata->loopback_rx_pkt)) {
+			/* Drain the FIFO without trusting the reported length as
+			 * a destination buffer size. Both buffers are word aligned.
+			 */
+			for (i = 0; i < rdsz; i++)
+				smsc911x_reg_read(pdata, RX_DATA_FIFO);
+			SMSC_WARN(pdata, hw, "Unexpected loopback size: %u",
+				  pktlength);
+			continue;
+		}
+
+		pdata->ops->rx_readfifo(pdata, (unsigned int *)bufp, rdsz);
